{"title":"2001 IMO Shortlist Problems/A6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Generalization\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Generalization</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Alternative_Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Alternative Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Alternative_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Alternative Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Resources\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Resources</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/A6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Prove that for all positive real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b29b358e825defa3e11b7d903d43ec31e5909a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" />,\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/9/b99abc5062d845cddcb97bb99675fe9a4de3a2ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {a}{\\sqrt {a^2 + 8bc}} + \\frac {b}{\\sqrt {b^2 + 8ca}} + \\frac {c}{\\sqrt {c^2 + 8ab}} \\geq 1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"330\" height=\"42\" /></center>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Generalization\">Generalization</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/A6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Generalization\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The leader of the Bulgarian team had come up with the following generalization to the inequality:\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/1/471af15648323ef1d44e3ee7252c1941f2ac8f40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {a}{\\sqrt {a^2 + kbc}} + \\frac {b}{\\sqrt {b^2 + kca}} + \\frac {c}{\\sqrt {c^2 + kab}} \\geq \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{1+k}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"385\" height=\"42\" /></center>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/A6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By AM-GM, we have\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/0/4b01b0b76c94b39e35abd7c5b6df01b63a8b16ac.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^4+y^4\\ge2\\sqrt{x^4y^4}=2x^2y^2 \\ \\dots \\ (\\text{I})\\]\" width=\"267\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>and\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/0/d406140f482e44d0aab647c54b3dc744b5566c15.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2x^2y^2+2\\ge2\\sqrt{4x^2y^2}=4xy \\ \\dots \\ (\\text{II})\\]\" width=\"286\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>which means\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/a/19afac8dfe9eb79f844fe84fa9141897d5d1fcc8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x^4+y^4)(x^4+y^4+2)\\overset{(\\text{I})}{\\ge}2x^2y^2(2x^2y^2+2)\\overset{(\\text{II})}{\\ge}8x^3y^3\\]\" width=\"404\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>as we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/d/75d7677c5da424fa50e62a1734daaf007be219e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x^4+y^4)(x^4+y^4+2)=(1+x^4+y^4)^2-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"341\" height=\"21\" />, we can reorganize the above inequality as follows\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/3/d8399cddbe32d88e322e9566114b8a407442f57b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(1+x^4+y^4)^2\\ge1+8x^3y^3 \\ \\Longleftrightarrow \\ 1+x^4+y^4\\ge\\sqrt{1+8x^3y^3}\\]\" width=\"468\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/7/427ebe407093f1c86fdced8eb48d92102c8321a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=(b/a)^{1/3}, \\ y=(c/a)^{1/3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"207\" height=\"23\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/2/f927241f21b17440446735f0c7a12714e43c1e2b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1+\\left(\\frac{b}{a}\\right)^{4/3}+\\left(\\frac{c}{a}\\right)^{4/3}\\ge\\sqrt{1+8\\cdot\\frac{b}{a}\\cdot\\frac{c}{a}}\\]\" width=\"304\" height=\"48\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/3/903b0c93e54e33c2136b214c60ce901a69ad790e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Longrightarrow\\frac{a^{4/3}+b^{4/3}+c^{4/3}}{a^{4/3}}\\ge\\frac{\\sqrt{a^2+8bc}}{a}\\]\" width=\"275\" height=\"40\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/5/265490f8c25d18d0fd290e8c54f29398d363e4fe.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Longrightarrow\\frac{a}{\\sqrt{a^2+8bc}}\\ge\\frac{a^{4/3}}{a^{4/3}+b^{4/3}+c^{4/3}}\\]\" width=\"275\" height=\"45\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/0/a300bc55ee98cb4be552338e99de4685010d8133.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Longrightarrow\\sum_{cyc}\\frac{a}{\\sqrt{a^2+8bc}}\\ge\\sum_{cyc}\\frac{a^{4/3}}{a^{4/3}+b^{4/3}+c^{4/3}}=1\\]\" width=\"366\" height=\"51\" />\n</p><p>Equality holds iff <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/6/566b9136144a62fac113ecbc8065793a74123238.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=b=c$\" width=\"74\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>or we can just note that:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/e/9febbdd2ed89885183ea0f304f2a6625490dc862.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{cyc}\\frac{a}{\\sqrt{a^2+8bc}}=1+\\sum_{cyc}\\frac{a^{7/3}\\left[\\left(\\frac{b}{a}\\right)^{2/3} - \\left(\\frac{c}{a}\\right)^{2/3}\\right]^2 \\left[ \\left(\\left(\\frac{b}{a}\\right)^{2/3} + \\left(\\frac{c}{a}\\right)^{2/3}\\right)^2 + 2 \\right] + 4a^{7/3}\\left(\\frac{bc}{a^2}\\right)^{2/3} \\left[\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{bc}{a^2}} - 1 \\right]^2}{\\left[1 + \\left(\\frac{b}{a}\\right)^{4/3} + \\left(\\frac{c}{a}\\right)^{4/3} + \\sqrt{1+\\frac{8bc}{a^2}}\\right](a^{4/3}+b^{4/3}+c^{4/3})\\sqrt{a^2+8bc}}\\ge1\\]\" width=\"815\" height=\"81\" />\n</p><p>--PanGibson\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Alternative_Solution_1\">Alternative Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/A6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Alternative Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We will use the Jenson's inequality. \n</p><p>Now, normalize the inequality by assuming <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/6/0463a97b25dc0b519ce3c0a1ba6ff2ab6f9f518f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"102\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Consider the function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/a/5ea176fdd3a4265d5b07d64de53b61ea90d6a52f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"87\" height=\"41\" />. Note that this function is convex and monotonically decreasing which implies that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/d/25d8ed1fc54739081e1cc984b300a5b1bd0a984f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &gt; b$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/d/50dc5135567209fe167625772089148b1513b27b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a) &lt; f(b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, we have\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/6/5b6e1e3c1e801583da8d50e5d70215f05725b870.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {a}{\\sqrt {a^2 + 8bc}} + \\frac {b}{\\sqrt {b^2 + 8ca}} + \\frac {c}{\\sqrt {c^2 + 8ab}} = af(a^2+8bc)+bf(b^2+8ca)+cf(c^2+8ab) \\geq f(a^3+b^3+c^3+24abc)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"860\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p>Thus, we only need to show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/0/170b0198c07c6a2582991757f045e78a2b6f686e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^3+b^3+c^3+24abc \\leq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"190\" height=\"17\" /> i.e.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/e/9be9b36efe3af400441ed55f7358473de13d6488.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^3+b^3+c^3+24abc \\leq (a+b+c)^3=a^3+b^3+c^3+3(a+b+c)(ab+bc+ca)-3abc\\]\" width=\"565\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/a/0babdb985058ff81b87004ff97bf0c2d3269b366.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[i.e.   (a+b+c)(ab+bc+ca) \\geq 9abc\\]\" width=\"276\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Which is true since\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/0/9405f95973dbc442c26fc6f46ef2709a698e77f5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(a+b+c)(ab+bc+ca) \\geq (3\\sqrt[3]{abc})(3\\sqrt[3]{a^{2}b^{2}c^{2}}) = 9abc\\]\" width=\"425\" height=\"22\" />\nThe last part follows by the AM-GM inequality.\n</p><p>Equality holds if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/6/566b9136144a62fac113ecbc8065793a74123238.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=b=c$\" width=\"74\" height=\"12\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Alternative_Solution_2\">Alternative Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/A6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Alternative Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By Carlson's Inequality, we can know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/0/d80ac482bda0fb14112eb9ec52859e4bff4b398a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Bigg(\\frac {a}{\\sqrt {a^2 + 8bc}} + \\frac {b}{\\sqrt {b^2 + 8ca}} + \\frac {c}{\\sqrt {c^2 + 8ab}}\\Bigg)\\Bigg(\\frac {a}{\\sqrt {a^2 + 8bc}} + \\frac {b}{\\sqrt {b^2 + 8ca}} + \\frac {c}{\\sqrt {c^2 + 8ab}}\\Bigg)\\Big((a^3+8abc)+(b^3+8abc)+(c^3+8abc)\\Big) \\ge (a+b+c)^3\\]\" width=\"990\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/c/35c4c81ea806746452e19ddeef472f81e78630f2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Bigg(\\frac {a}{\\sqrt {a^2 + 8bc}} + \\frac {b}{\\sqrt {b^2 + 8ca}} + \\frac {c}{\\sqrt {c^2 + 8ab}}\\Bigg)^2 \\ge \\frac{(a+b+c)^3}{a^3+b^3+c^3+24abc}\\]\" width=\"493\" height=\"57\" />\n</p><p>On the other hand, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/f/11f2a8b9b6b105bcd6f39264992636c41616475e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3a^2b+3b^2c+3c^2a \\ge 9abc\\]\" width=\"202\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/7/9a792ba06e4f4c8b888251d84e135dd96329db37.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3ab^2+3bc^2+3ca^2 \\ge 9abc\\]\" width=\"202\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/8/4e8de5887d443e9638027642af3383f4c972cbb3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(a+b+c)^3 = a^3+b^3+c^3+3(a^2b+ab^2+a^2c+ac^2+b^2c+bc^2)+6abc \\ge a^3+b^3+c^3+24abc\\]\" width=\"634\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/d/3ad9ada38beb6b7279d4eb6869718730490856e0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Bigg(\\frac {a}{\\sqrt {a^2 + 8bc}} + \\frac {b}{\\sqrt {b^2 + 8ca}} + \\frac {c}{\\sqrt {c^2 + 8ab}}\\Bigg)^2 \\ge \\frac{(a+b+c)^3}{a^3+b^3+c^3+24abc} \\ge 1\\]\" width=\"527\" height=\"57\" />\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/9/d190bf8c453b1f41e2605df63c2d96b35e33259c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac {a}{\\sqrt {a^2 + 8bc}} + \\frac {b}{\\sqrt {b^2 + 8ca}} + \\frac {c}{\\sqrt {c^2 + 8ab}} \\ge 1\\]\" width=\"324\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p>-- Haozhe Yang\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Resources\">Resources</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Shortlist_Problems/A6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Resources\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Shortlist_Problems\" title=\"2001 IMO Shortlist Problems\">2001 IMO Shortlist Problems</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/viewtopic.php?t=17451\">Discussion on AOPS/MathLinks</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017090738\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.026 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.039 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 177/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7651/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:7181:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017090738 and revision id 282532. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}